    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `find_candidates` in `app/catalog.py`. It makes one `list_models` call with `search=name_fragment`, `pipeline_tag=task`, `sort=\"downloads\"` and `limit=limit`, so the Hub does the filtering, sorting and limiting and only one page of `limit` results comes back. Both tests pass with `pytest -q`: the existing one and a new one I added in `tests/test_catalog.py`. The new test uses a fake API, so it only checks that the right arguments are sent. It never contacted the real Hub, so the actual results haven't been checked.\n\nChoices you may want to change:\n\n- **Optional `api` argument:** like `org_models` and `model_stats`, the function takes an optional `api: HfApi | None = None` so tests can pass in a fake.\n- **Public models only:** the function passes `token=False`, so the request is sent without your saved Hugging Face login. Without it, private models your token can see could end up in the shortlist. The catch is that these calls get the lower rate limits the Hub gives to requests without a login. Remove `token=False` if you'd rather have the higher limits.\n- **Sort order:** huggingface_hub 2.0.0 no longer has a `direction` parameter, so the most-downloaded-first order relies on the Hub sorting downloads from highest to lowest by default.\n- **Name matching:** `search` matches the fragment anywhere in the full model id (`owner/name`), not just the part after the slash."
